1
00:00:00,628 --> 00:00:06,328
(Amy:)Sheldon, sometimes people seek the comfort
of physical contact in moments like this.

2
00:00:11,205 --> 00:00:15,335
(Sheldon:)I am not flying back to Texas
just so my mom can give me a hug.

3
00:00:17,678 --> 00:00:20,268
(Amy:)Okay. Well, what I think is going on here...

4
00:00:20,481 --> 00:00:23,181
(Amy:)...is you have a pathological need
for closure.

5
00:00:23,384 --> 00:00:25,444
(Sheldon:)Oh. That's nonsense.

6
00:00:25,653 --> 00:00:29,683
(Sheldon:)You tell me stories about your day
all the time. I don't care how they end.

7
00:00:32,026 --> 00:00:34,786
(Amy:)You know, I might be able
to help you with this.

8
00:00:34,995 --> 00:00:37,725
There's a field of behavioral neuroscience
that examines...

9
00:00:37,898 --> 00:00:41,458
(Amy:)...ways to retrain your neural pathways
so stuff like this bothers you less.

10
00:00:41,635 --> 00:00:44,365
(Sheldon:)But I just told you,
I don't have a problem with closure.

11
00:00:45,106 --> 00:00:59,026
- You sure about that?
- Quite sure.

